Bandwidth

Single control: full stop widens the bandwidth; comma narrows it.
Separate edges: p selects Low Cut, then alternates Upper Cut and Low Cut.
Full stop raises the selected edge; comma lowers it. Selecting an edge reads its current value without changing it.
Each adjustment is applied immediately and confirmed by reading the radio.
From Default, full stop selects the narrowest numeric width; comma selects the widest.
h reads this help. q finishes with Done and keeps changes, returning to Filters.
Not Supported means no bandwidth control is available for this radio and mode; YAC returns to Filters without changing anything.
